# fixture: walking and collision in the room, talking to the helper (sets a flag), the TV bg (two pages).
# Timings (real World/VM, 30 Hz): walk 8 ticks per tile; a new direction first turns (2 ticks);
# walking into a wall or object bumps in place; text prints 1 char per 2 ticks.
#
# new game: spawn in the room; the onFrame intro starts once the fade-in ends
0 assert map fixture:ROOM
0 assert position fixture:ROOM 14 16
0 assert flag fixture:FLAG_NEW_GAME_DONE true
12 assert message open
80 press a
82 release a
86 assert message closed
86 assert var fixture:VAR_ROOM_INTRO 1
# up one tile (already facing up: no turn)
90 press up
92 release up
100 assert position fixture:ROOM 14 15
# left is the table (12..13, 14..15): turn, then bump in place
100 press left
120 release left
130 assert position fixture:ROOM 14 15
# right four tiles to 18,15, below the helper
130 press right
160 release right
170 assert position fixture:ROOM 18 15
# up into the helper: turn and bump, no step
170 press up
190 release up
200 assert position fixture:ROOM 18 15
# talk: the flag is set at once, the message waits for A
200 press a
202 release a
206 assert flag fixture:FLAG_TALKED_TO_HELPER true
206 assert message open
320 assert message open
320 press a
322 release a
326 assert message closed
# talk again: the other branch, flag unchanged
330 press a
332 release a
336 assert message open
420 press a
422 release a
426 assert message closed
426 assert flag fixture:FLAG_TALKED_TO_HELPER true
# to the TV: left to 14,15, up to 14,13, left to 12,13, face up
430 press left
464 release left
474 assert position fixture:ROOM 14 15
474 press up
492 release up
502 assert position fixture:ROOM 14 13
502 press left
520 release left
530 assert position fixture:ROOM 12 13
530 press up
531 release up
# the TV bg at 12,12 faces up; its text has two pages ({clear})
540 press a
542 release a
546 assert message open
620 press a
622 release a
626 assert message open
680 press a
682 release a
686 assert message closed
686 assert position fixture:ROOM 12 13
